message.content:
{
  "42": {
    "document_id": "42",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Collins and Lott announce a negotiated agreement on FEMA restructuring whose provisions 'will be included in a bill introduced today.' The legislation has only been introduced - nothing has passed or been enacted - so under negative clarification (3) (introductions of legislation that has not passed) this is advocacy/position-taking on national policy machinery, not a delivered particularized benefit to their states."
  },
  "714": {
    "document_id": "714",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Although framed as a column honoring U.S. Marshals, the senator makes an explicit role statement: 'I helped secure more than $3 billion in the fiscal year 2006 Homeland Security appropriations bill for ICE's domestic enforcement efforts, as well as funding for 250 additional criminal investigators.' This is exactly the type of explicit 'I helped secure' funding claim that clarification (2) says to include, and it is tied to law enforcement protecting Idahoans. The ceremonial framing does not negate the embedded appropriations credit claim."
  },
  "794": {
    "document_id": "794",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Much of the release is position-taking (Iraq, taxes, intelligence), but Bond states: 'The new federal highway bill, which Bond co-authored, is providing Missouri with much-needed resources, including $1 billion in new money - more than $4 billion in total funding.' Under clarification (4), touting a previously enacted bill the senator authored/co-authored, framed as delivering concrete benefits (transportation funding) to his state, is credit-claiming."
  },
  "805": {
    "document_id": "805",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Shelby announces that the Department of Homeland Security will release $3,510 to the Homewood Fire Department in Alabama through the Assistance to Firefighters Grant Program. Under clarification (1), a senator's own announcement of a federal grant benefiting his state is itself a credit-claiming vehicle, even without an explicit 'I secured it' statement."
  },
  "1257": {
    "document_id": "1257",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "DeWine announces a $105,550 federal grant to the Parma (Ohio) Fire Department and explicitly claims responsibility: he 'wrote and passed the FIRE Act,' 'helped secure approximately $650 million for the FIRE Act,' and the grant comes 'through Sen. DeWine's bill.' This matches clarification (1), (2), and (5) - announcement of a grant plus explicit role statements and touting of past funding wins for the state."
  },
  "1325": {
    "document_id": "1325",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Dole's floor statement is entirely about the judicial nominations process, attacking Democrats for filibustering nominees and defending the 'constitutional option.' It is pure position-taking and criticism of the opposing party on a national policy/procedural issue, with no claim of responsibility for any delivered governmental benefit. Falls under negative clarification (1) and (2)."
  },
  "1749": {
    "document_id": "1749",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Hutchison announces she has 'signed on as an original cosponsor' of the Veterans Housing Benefits Enhancement Act, which was 'introduced today.' Under negative clarification (3), cosponsorship of legislation that has not passed or been adopted is advocacy/position-taking, not credit-claiming - this is the boundary case illustrated by the Thune/Clinton negative example."
  },
  "1897": {
    "document_id": "1897",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Martinez's statement takes a position on pending offshore drilling legislation - praising Putnam, refusing to support the Pombo bill in its current form, and threatening to join a filibuster unless the buffer is extended. It is position-taking on a bill that has not passed, with no delivered benefit claimed. Negative clarification (1) and (3) apply."
  },
  "1927": {
    "document_id": "1927",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Snowe announces that $8.1 million for the Portsmouth Naval Shipyard was included in the FY2006 appropriations bill that 'passed the Senate today,' noting 'This funding was requested by Snowe and Sen. Susan Collins.' This is classic appropriations credit-claiming: an explicit role statement ('requested by') plus announcement of federal funds for a Maine facility, matching clarification (1) and (2) and the Talent positive example."
  },
  "2335": {
    "document_id": "2335",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Bayh's release announces an essay contest to honor 'Outstanding Hoosier Dads,' with winners entered into the Congressional Record. This is ceremonial recognition of constituents, excluded by negative clarification (4) (commemorations, resolutions honoring others, awards presented to constituents - cf. the Lugar award negative example). The passing reference to the Responsible Fatherhood Act is background advocacy about fatherhood, not a framed claim of delivered particularized benefits, and does not change the release's commemorative character."
  },
  "2869": {
    "document_id": "2869",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Jeffords' statement explains why he voted for the Kerry and Levin amendments on Iraq and criticizes the Administration's war policy. Under negative clarification (2), explanations or defenses of the senator's own votes without a claim of producing a beneficial outcome are excluded, and criticism of the administration is excluded under negative clarification (1)."
  },
  "3252": {
    "document_id": "3252",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "The headline announces 'SENATE ADOPTS NELSON AMENDMENT,' and Nelson claims the adopted amendment as his own ('his amendment... passed on a bipartisan vote of 72 to 26'), framing it as 'a victory for Nebraska's ranchers, for Nebraska's beef.' Under clarification (2) and (4), claiming responsibility for an adopted amendment framed as delivering benefits to a favored constituency counts as credit-claiming, even though the underlying appropriations bill still faces conference."
  },
  "4022": {
    "document_id": "4022",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Kennedy's floor statement introduces a 'Medicare for All' bill, critiques the Administration and Republicans on health policy, and urges support. This is introduction of legislation and national policy position-taking - nothing has passed or been delivered. Negative clarifications (1) and (3) apply: 'merely introducing, cosponsoring, or advocating a bill does not count.'"
  },
  "4122": {
    "document_id": "4122",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "This release announces a Permanent Subcommittee on Investigations hearing into Medicaid providers owing back taxes. It is an oversight/investigation announcement with no achieved result claimed for the current matter, excluded by negative clarifications (5) (announcements of hearings) and (6) (oversight statements and investigations). The touting of past increases in tax levy collections refers to general taxpayer savings across the federal government, not particularized benefits delivered to a state, district, or favored constituency, so it does not meet the definition of credit-claiming."
  },
  "4184": {
    "document_id": "4184",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Kyl announces that he 'co-sponsored legislation' (an amendment to the Budget Resolution) that 'calls for' 2,000 new Border Patrol agents and $352 million. There is no claim the amendment was adopted or passed - it is only a sponsorship/advocacy announcement. Under negative clarification (3), introductions and cosponsorships of legislation that has not been adopted are position-taking, not credit-claiming."
  },
  "4207": {
    "document_id": "4207",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "The core of the release is Cornyn's letter to Secretary Chertoff asking DHS to 'give due consideration' to a levee proposal - a letter pressuring an agency with no achieved result claimed, excluded by negative clarification (6). His amendment merely required IBWC to 'report to Congress' (a procedural reporting requirement, not delivered funds or a project for Texas), and his appropriations letter is only a request. No concrete benefit to Texas is claimed as delivered."
  },
  "4295": {
    "document_id": "4295",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Although the release primarily announces the introduction of a new FMAP bill, Murkowski explicitly touts a past win: she 'helped win a two-year change in the Economic Growth Reconciliation Act... that provided the state with an additional $34.11 million above the traditional Medicaid formula amount.' This is a claim of personal responsibility for an enacted provision that delivered concrete federal funds to Alaska, squarely within clarification (4) (touting enacted provisions she championed, framed as delivering benefits) and (5) (touting past wins of funding for the state)."
  },
  "4508": {
    "document_id": "4508",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Lott announces that 300 travel trailers and 100 mobile homes are being moved to South Mississippi for Katrina victims, and explicitly ties the favorable FEMA action to his own intervention: 'The announcement follows the Senator's Monday appeal to President Bush to authorize the immediate transport of available trailers.' This matches clarification (1) (senator's own announcement of federal resources benefiting his state) and (3) (claiming his appeal produced a favorable administration decision)."
  },
  "4677": {
    "document_id": "4677",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "At a subcommittee hearing, Hutchison asked questions about BRAC, received assurances it is on schedule, and said she is 'encouraged to see $18 million in the emergency supplemental for facilities at Fort Hood.' She does not claim to have secured that funding - she only welcomes it, and it remains a pending budget request, not a delivered benefit. This fits negative clarification (7) (welcoming favorable developments without any claim of responsibility and without a final delivered benefit) and (5) (hearing activity)."
  },
  "4774": {
    "document_id": "4774",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Although the release's purpose is to urge conferees to retain the provision, it rests on a claimed legislative milestone: 'the Senate unanimously approved an amendment offered by Senators Bayh and Durbin,' which Bayh calls 'his legislation' and frames as delivering benefits ('will provide crucial assistance' to Guard and Reserve families facing the Patriot Penalty). Under clarification (4) and the rule that legislative milestones count when the senator claims responsibility for an adopted amendment, this is credit-claiming, unlike mere introduction or cosponsorship. I note some ambiguity because the benefit is not yet final (conference pending), but the codebook explicitly treats an adopted amendment as sufficient."
  }
}

{
  "817": {
    "document_id": "817",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Collins announces a hearing on the Social Security Fairness Act she sponsored and her testimony in support of it. The bill has not passed or been adopted; per negative clarification (3), sponsoring/advocating legislation that has not passed is position-taking, not credit-claiming, even though it would deliver benefits. No achieved governmental outcome is claimed."
  },
  "871": {
    "document_id": "871",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Salazar questions Interior Secretary Norton about proposed budget cuts to PILT, LWCF, and Park Service rules. This is oversight and criticism of the administration with no achieved result claimed. Negative clarification (6) excludes oversight statements and pressure on agencies when no achieved result is claimed."
  },
  "1118": {
    "document_id": "1118",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Carper's statement explains and defends his vote against the constitutional amendment banning gay marriage. Under negative clarifications (1) and (2), position statements on national policy and explanations of one's own votes without a claim of producing a beneficial outcome are excluded."
  },
  "1177": {
    "document_id": "1177",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Pryor and Chambliss call on the Air Force to reimburse unpaid subcontractors and announce they will keep pressuring the Secretary of the Air Force. No favorable decision or reimbursement has been achieved. Negative clarification (6) excludes letters/statements pressuring agencies when no achieved result is claimed."
  },
  "1230": {
    "document_id": "1230",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Harkin and Hatch announce the FDA's long-sought publication of GMP regulations, noting they authored DSHEA and 'have been pushing the FDA to publish GMPs for more than a decade.' This frames the favorable agency decision as the product of their sustained pressure, fitting clarification (3) (claims that the senator's pressure produced a favorable agency decision), analogous to the Landrieu positive example where an agency acts after prolonged senatorial pressure."
  },
  "1320": {
    "document_id": "1320",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Hutchison announces passage of an emergency appropriations bill containing $3 billion for drought and wildfire relief benefiting Texas and says 'I am pleased to help secure this funding.' This is an explicit role statement (clarification (2)) combined with an announced delivered appropriation (clarification (1)) - textbook credit-claiming."
  },
  "1747": {
    "document_id": "1747",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "The release touts that 'the U.S. Senate has approved legislation by Sen. Robert C. Byrd' boosting funding for the Youth ChalleNGe program, including West Virginia's Mountaineer ChalleNGe Academy. Under clarification (4), touting provisions the senator authored in a bill that passed a chamber, framed as delivering benefits, counts as credit-claiming. The bill passed the Senate 98-0."
  },
  "1862": {
    "document_id": "1862",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Baucus and Tester announce $12.5 million for Butte military projects included in the Defense Appropriations Bill, saying they 'delivered on their promise to secure federal funding' and 'were proud to go to bat for these dollars.' Under clarifications (1) and (2), a senator's own announcement of appropriations benefiting their state, with explicit role statements, is credit-claiming - mirroring the Talent positive example."
  },
  "2026": {
    "document_id": "2026",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "The release reports Judiciary Committee passage of the Leahy-Specter data privacy bill, which 'now moves to the full Senate.' Committee passage is not passage by a chamber, and the bill's benefits are general national consumer protections, not particularized benefits to Vermont. Under negative clarification (3) and the clarification that milestones count only for bills actually passed/adopted, this is legislative advocacy, not credit-claiming."
  },
  "2627": {
    "document_id": "2627",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Talent announces that 'the Senate has approved his request for $1.5 million' for a University of Missouri research center, with university officials thanking him for securing the money. This matches the codebook's own positive example: explicit role statement plus an announced appropriation benefiting his state (clarifications (1) and (2))."
  },
  "2675": {
    "document_id": "2675",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Dodd, Lieberman, and Simmons met with BRAC commissioners to argue against closing Sub Base New London, but no favorable decision has been reached - Dodd says 'until we reach the finish line and hopefully prevail our work isn't done.' Under negative clarifications (6) and (7), advocacy and pressure without an achieved, delivered benefit is not credit-claiming."
  },
  "3271": {
    "document_id": "3271",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "The release touts unanimous Senate passage of the Financial Services Regulatory Relief Act, 'authored by Idaho Senator Mike Crapo,' and frames it as delivering benefits (reduced regulatory burden, better customer service, relief for community banks and credit unions). Under clarification (4), touting a bill the senator authored that passed a chamber, framed as delivering benefits, is credit-claiming."
  },
  "3477": {
    "document_id": "3477",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Cornyn comments on the Senate confirmation of Carol Dinkins to chair the Privacy and Civil Liberties Oversight Board. This is a nomination announcement without any claim of delivering a benefit; negative clarification (5) excludes announcements of nominations without claimed benefits. Cornyn claims no responsibility for a particularized governmental outcome."
  },
  "3501": {
    "document_id": "3501",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Tester expresses disappointment that the Air Force is targeting Malmstrom's missiles and vows to 'continue to fight' and 'work toward getting another mission.' This is advocacy/position-taking in response to an adverse development with no achieved benefit, excluded by negative clarifications (6) and (7)."
  },
  "3534": {
    "document_id": "3534",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Domenici praises President Bush's gasoline price plan and calls for a unified national energy approach. Under negative clarification (1), position statements on national policy, including praise of the President, are excluded. Domenici claims no responsibility for any delivered benefit to New Mexico or any constituency."
  },
  "3560": {
    "document_id": "3560",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "The Arkansas delegation announces $877,749 in HUD grants to Arkansas public housing agencies, listing each recipient and amount. Under clarification (1), a senator's own announcement of federal grants benefiting their state is itself a credit-claiming vehicle, even without an explicit 'I secured it' statement."
  },
  "3729": {
    "document_id": "3729",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Grassley announces that President Bush named Matt Dummermuth interim U.S. Attorney for the Northern District of Iowa and notes Dummermuth was among Grassley's nominees. This is a nomination/personnel announcement without a claimed particularized benefit; negative clarification (5) excludes announcements of nominations without claimed benefits."
  },
  "3744": {
    "document_id": "3744",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Inouye announces the CDC's decision to establish a field station in Hawaii, a favorable agency decision/facility benefiting his state - his own announcement is a credit-claiming vehicle under clarification (1). He also explicitly notes a past win: 'at Senator Inouye's request' the CDC previously established an occupational health center at UH-Hilo, fitting clarification (2) and (5)."
  },
  "3845": {
    "document_id": "3845",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Bayh's statement responds to OPEC's decision and promotes his introduced energy bill (S.2025), urging Congress to pass it. The bill has not passed, so under negative clarification (3) this is advocacy/position-taking on national policy (negative clarification (1)), not credit-claiming."
  },
  "4531": {
    "document_id": "4531",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Thune and Clinton announce they have introduced legislation to extend child care benefits for fallen soldiers' families. This matches the codebook's negative example exactly: merely introducing legislation, without passage or adoption, is advocacy/position-taking under negative clarification (3)."
  }
}

{
  "133": {
    "document_id": "133",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Kerry's statement criticizes the administration's handling of the Dubai Ports deal in light of the Israel boycott revelation. It is purely an attack on the administration and a policy position - no claim of responsibility for any delivered benefit. Negative clarification (1): position statements including blame of the administration."
  },
  "214": {
    "document_id": "214",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "A Pearl Harbor remembrance honoring those who served. Negative clarification (4): commemorations and remembrances are excluded - no government benefit is claimed or delivered."
  },
  "299": {
    "document_id": "299",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Alexander is named 'Hero of the Taxpayer' by Americans for Tax Reform based on his voting record. Negative clarification (4) explicitly excludes 'third-party awards recognizing the senator's voting record.' No government action or delivered benefit is claimed."
  },
  "490": {
    "document_id": "490",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Webb's statement on the NIE is a critique of the Bush administration's refusal to engage adversaries - a foreign policy position. Negative clarification (1): position statements on national policy, including criticism of the administration, with no claim of producing any benefit."
  },
  "630": {
    "document_id": "630",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Dodd comments on the Connecticut impact of Bush's proposed budget and urges higher priority for submarine production ('needs to make... a higher priority'). This is advocacy/position-taking on a pending budget proposal; no achieved or delivered benefit is claimed. Negative clarifications (1) and (6)."
  },
  "721": {
    "document_id": "721",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Reid's statement on the Iraqi elections salutes troops and demands the administration produce a strategy - a national security policy position with criticism of the President. No particularized benefit or claim of responsibility. Negative clarification (1)."
  },
  "773": {
    "document_id": "773",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "The Senate passed a resolution, co-introduced by McCaskill, honoring the life of former Senator Eagleton. Even though the resolution passed, negative clarification (4) explicitly excludes 'resolutions honoring others.' It confers no government benefit and claims no policy outcome."
  },
  "1060": {
    "document_id": "1060",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Nelson announces Senate passage of SCHIP reauthorization and says he 'joined 66 of his colleagues in supporting the measure,' touting benefits for Nebraska children and noting an included sense-of-the-senate amendment he merely cosponsored. This is primarily a vote explanation without a claim of personal responsibility for producing the outcome; the codebook's milestone rule requires an authored/championed/adopted provision, and negative clarification (3) states cosponsorship does not count, while negative clarification (2) excludes vote explanations. I weighed that the bill passed a chamber, but Nelson claims no specific role in producing it."
  },
  "1086": {
    "document_id": "1086",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Dayton 'applauded' Senate passage of additional LIHEAP funding but claims no responsibility for it; his own four cosponsored amendments were all defeated. Welcoming a favorable development without a claim of responsibility is excluded (negative clarification 7), and cosponsoring (defeated) amendments does not count (negative clarification 3)."
  },
  "1155": {
    "document_id": "1155",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Leahy claims shared responsibility for an adopted legislative milestone: 'we painstakingly built two of the four pillars of a successful trust fund... With the unanimous adoption of the Leahy Hatch medical criteria amendment this committee reached consensus on the proper standards for determining legitimate victims.' The codebook's clarification (2) and (4) count adopted amendments - 'my amendment was adopted' - when framed as delivering benefits, and here it is framed as the mechanism delivering compensation to asbestos victims. I acknowledge ambiguity: the broader statement is advocacy for pending legislation and the trust fund never became law, but the explicit claim of an adopted, named amendment meets the codebook's milestone rule, unlike mere introduction or cosponsorship."
  },
  "1313": {
    "document_id": "1313",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Lieberman expresses frustration at the House's refusal to take up the DC voting rights bill and commends Utah officials and other senators. This is advocacy/position-taking on legislation that has not passed; no benefit was delivered and Lieberman claims no achieved result. Negative clarifications (1) and (3)."
  },
  "1827": {
    "document_id": "1827",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Lugar announces that provisions of his Good Samaritan Hunger Relief Act 'will be included' in the pending Grassley-Baucus Katrina tax relief package and thanks the chairmen for including them. The codebook's milestone rule counts legislative achievements only when 'actually adopted or passed'; here the package has not passed any chamber - inclusion is prospective - and no benefit (the food-donation tax deduction) has been delivered. This is advocacy regarding pending legislation akin to negative clarification (3). I note ambiguity: inclusion in a leadership package resembles an adopted provision, but the future tense and lack of passage keep it from satisfying the milestone rule. The 2003 Senate passage cited is historical and never became law."
  },
  "2003": {
    "document_id": "2003",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Clinton announces that the Air Force will place a new Predator squadron in New York, touting it as an 'additional mission for New York' with potential for 'high tech economic growth.' Clarification (1): the senator's own announcement of a military mission/basing decision benefiting her state is itself a credit-claiming vehicle even without an explicit 'I secured it,' and her statement that 'the Air Force recognizes that New York can support this additional mission' reinforces the claim."
  },
  "2143": {
    "document_id": "2143",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Murray's statement mourns the passing of former Washington Democratic Party chairwoman Karen Marchioro. Negative clarification (4): condolences and remembrances are excluded. No government action or benefit is claimed."
  },
  "3047": {
    "document_id": "3047",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "The release announces USDA's decision to purchase up to 80 million pounds of potatoes under Section 32 - a favorable agency decision benefiting Idaho growers - and explicitly ties it to the senator's action: 'On March 15, 2005, the Idaho Congressional Delegation wrote the Secretary requesting this action.' Clarification (3): claims that the senator's letter/appeal produced a favorable agency decision count; the definition allows shared (delegation) responsibility."
  },
  "3201": {
    "document_id": "3201",
    "label": "1",
    "explanation": "Talent announces USDA's disaster designation for most of Missouri, unlocking emergency loans and assistance, and explicitly states he 'worked with USDA officials to expedite the approval of the Governor's request'; he also references his earlier announcement of $1,078,500 in ECP funds for Missouri. Clarifications (1) and (3): announcements of disaster declarations benefiting the state and claims of producing a favorable agency decision are credit-claiming."
  },
  "3914": {
    "document_id": "3914",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Frist's statement credits 'Republican economic policies' for job growth and attacks Democrats. Negative clarification (8): general credit to one's party or broad national policies is excluded; it is a partisan position statement with no particularized benefit to Tennessee."
  },
  "3950": {
    "document_id": "3950",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "In the provided text, Harkin only 'hopes' the new regional diabetes facility will help Iowans; there is no claim that he secured funding or any delivered federal benefit for the center. The reference to his authoring the HeLP America Act concerns introduced/pending legislation, which negative clarification (3) excludes. No credit-claiming element is present in the text as given."
  },
  "4124": {
    "document_id": "4124",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Kennedy commends President Bush's call for comprehensive immigration reform and urges congressional action. This is a position statement on national policy praising another actor - no claim of responsibility for any delivered benefit. Negative clarification (1)."
  },
  "4344": {
    "document_id": "4344",
    "label": "0",
    "explanation": "Salazar announces he 'joined a bipartisan group of colleagues' supporting the PATRIOT Act compromise. This is a position statement/vote explanation on national policy with no particularized benefit to Colorado and no claim that he produced the deal - joining is not an authored/championed/adopted milestone. Negative clarifications (1) and (2)."
  }
}
